        <dc:title>Gone Tomorrow</dc:title>
        <dc:creator opf:file-as="Child, Lee" opf:role="aut">Lee Child</dc:creator>
        <dc:contributor opf:file-as="calibre" opf:role="bkp">calibre (1.48.0) [http://calibre-ebook.com]</dc:contributor>
        <dc:date>2010-08-15T15:50:12+00:00</dc:date>
        <dc:description>SUMMARY: Susan Mark, the fifth passenger, had a big secret, and her plain little life was being watched in Washington, and California, and Afghanistan-by dozens of people with one thing in common: They're all lying to Reacher. A little. A lot. Or just enough to get him killed. A race has begun through the streets of Manhattan, a maze crowded with violent, skilled soldiers on all sides of a shadow war. For Jack Reacher, a man who trusts no one and likes it that way, the finish line comes when you finally get face-to-face and look your worst enemy in the eye.</dc:description>
